  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One process, one registry",
      "items": [
        "This is the HTTP operation path. The web UI, CLI, pipeline and agent use the same operation registry. Reader threads belong to the same Bun process.",
        "POST /api/p/:project/:op. A bearer token, session cookie or verified local-owner request supplies the identity facts. Cookie and local admission require the same origin.",
        "Sources: src/surfaces/http.ts:230\u2013248, 410\u2013461, 819\u2013846; src/server/ops/registry.ts:1\u20132; src/server/ops/readers.ts:154\u2013160."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Reads and writes are alternatives",
      "items": [
        "Read: invokeAsync checks capability before dispatch. The worker runs invoke, resolves the caller and grants, validates input and reads in one snapshot. With no ready worker, the read runs inline on the reader connection.",
        "Write: after waiting at the gate, begin the transaction, resolve authority, check capability and parse input. makeCtx takes project.seq + 1. Domain modules own their tables; examples stamp seq or rev from ctx.seq.",
        "Sources: src/server/ops/registry.ts:169\u2013239, 277\u2013344, 363\u2013419; src/server/ops/read-worker.ts:103\u2013148; src/server/ops/readers.ts:108\u2013125; src/server/kernel/ctx.ts:231\u2013259."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Commit, notify and reply",
      "items": [
        "When cmd is supplied, record its request and result before commit. A finished project command retried unchanged by the same actor returns the stored reply and writes nothing; changed content under that id is refused.",
        "A fresh report has two transactions: accept, then apply. Each commit takes a sequence number and publishes a change. The write branch above shows an ordinary command.",
        "The event uses a separate, already open GET /api/p/:project/events stream with read access. It is a change hint; a client that misses it refetches. The reply carries the common security headers; HSTS depends on HTTPS.",
        "Sources: src/server/ops/registry.ts:286\u2013344; src/server/ops/writes.ts:362\u2013372; src/surfaces/http.ts:583\u2013646; src/surfaces/headers.ts:165\u2013184; src/surfaces/with-headers.ts:14\u201316."
      ]
    }
  ]
